  "pairs": [],
  "limitations": [
    "Duration mismatch: the same campaign is often published as a 30 s cut and a 60 s cut. A pair whose runtimes differ by more than 10% of the longer one is marked durationMismatch and reported both inside and outside the durationMatched statistics; it is a different edit, not a delivery artefact.",
    "Different cuts of the same work: when the duration matches but cuts per minute differ by more than 50%, the pair is a retimed or alternate edit. It is flagged cutRateDivergence and cut out of the cutRateConsistent statistics rather than counted as measurement error.",
    "Host loudness normalisation: YouTube and Vimeo normalise playback loudness. LUFS/LRA agreement therefore validates the delivered stream, not the master; a mastering difference can be flattened or invented by the host.",
    "Partial lanes: a work with census on one site and only audio on the other is a partial pair. It is counted and paired only on the lane both sides share; it is never averaged into a metric one side lacks.",
    "Zero-valued metrics: a relative difference is defined as (A - B) / max(|A|, |B|). When both values are zero the denominator is zero, so the relative difference is null and counted under relativeZeroDenominators rather than coerced to zero or to infinity.",
    "Census cut candidates are ffmpeg scene-score exceedances, not verified edits; fast motion, flashes, transitions and compression can cross the threshold. Strobe-flagged records are never pooled with non-strobe records for cutsPerMinute.",
    "Luma and saturation are display-RGB proxies at the decoded rendition size, not scene-linear light or calibrated colour; different resolutions and codecs shift them independently of the work.",
    "Coverage gap in this snapshot: 248 works appear on two or more sites, but 0 have numeric census or audio evidence on two of them. The figure of 219 describes works with a *selected row* on more than one site, not works that were measured twice. The pair statistics above are therefore empty, and the honest reading is that this corpus cannot yet answer the cross-site question."
  ]
